{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>Akh on the fifteenth day.</b> This 'akh' is a restriction. What does it restrict? The festival of Pesach — one is not obligated to remain in Jerusalem for more than one day, because of the preoccupation with harvesting barley. And likewise at Atzeret, because of the preoccupation with harvesting wheat, so that one may gather in his grain lest it spoil. But on the festival of Sukkot, when everything has been gathered into the house, he is obligated to rejoice for eight days."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:48.343162848Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}